---
title: New order
---
<script>
  // The whole form is derived, and now that includes the FIELD LIST. Look for a
  // field name, a type, an enum value, a required flag, a control choice or the
  // name of the customers resource in this file — none of them are here, because
  // all of them are in db/schema.lite.
  //
  // This page used to carry ~90 lines of state machine (`errors` / `shown` /
  // `typed` / `visible`, a `check()`, an `onInput`, an `onLeave`, a `saving`
  // flag and a `save()` that unwrapped a ResourceValidationError by hand), and
  // then ~40 lines of a hand-rolled `Object.entries(fields)` loop deciding
  // control-per-type with the foreign key lifted out. The first became <Form>
  // in @frontierjs/ui; the second became <Form>'s generated field list, over
  // the control table in sierra's field-rules.js. Both are stated once there
  // rather than re-derived in every app.
  //
  // There is not even an exclusion left. `trackingCode` is written by the
  // book-courier job and a person must never be offered a box for it — which
  // the schema now says in the only place it could be true: `@system` on the
  // column. It reaches the browser as `readOnly`, the control table has no
  // control for a readOnly field, and the form does not render one. This page
  // used to carry the repo's only hard-coded field name for that (FJS-095).
  import { orders } from '../../resources/Order.mesa'
  import { goto } from '@frontierjs/sierra/router'
  import { session } from '../../session.js'

  import Alert         from '@frontierjs/ui/components/feedback/Alert.mesa'
  import Button        from '@frontierjs/ui/components/forms/Button.mesa'
  import Form          from '@frontierjs/ui/components/forms/Form.mesa'
  import SectionHeader from '@frontierjs/ui/components/display/SectionHeader.mesa'

  $: session.level

  // `var`, not `const`: a gate level comes off the schema and never changes,
  // so a snapshot is what it is. Read straight in the template it is still a
  // one-time read, only silently.
  var createLevel = orders.gate.create
</script>

<SectionHeader title="New order" level={1}>
  {#snippet action()}
    <Button variant="ghost" href="/orders/">Back to list</Button>
  {/snippet}
</SectionHeader>

{#if session.level < createLevel}
  <Alert tone="warning">
    Not signed in at level {createLevel}. <code>@@gate</code> wants that
    to create, so this will come back 401 — which is the point: the button is
    NOT disabled, because the server is the thing that decides.
  </Alert>
{/if}

<!--
  <Form> with no children IS the form. It renders every writable column in
  schema order, each with the control its type implies: `status` is a select
  over the enum's members, `customerId` is a picker whose rows come from the
  Customer relation, `total` is a number, the rest are text. It also owns
  submit, in-flight state, the reveal rule and the map from a rejection to a
  message under the right control — including the 401 above, which arrives with
  no field information and lands in the form-level Alert.

  It also sets `novalidate` itself. That is load-bearing and used to be a
  hand-written attribute with a paragraph next to it: the kit's controls put a
  real `required` on the input, so the browser's own constraint validation
  refuses to fire a submit at all while a required field is empty — silently in
  a headless browser, and with "Please fill out this field" in a real one. The
  message this app shows is the one authored in db/schema.lite.
-->
<Form
  resource={orders}
  class="card"
  style="max-width: 32rem"
  ondone={() => goto('/orders/')}
>
  <!--
    `slot="actions"` rather than children — children would mean "I am writing
    this form myself" and turn the generated list off. <Form> puts them in a
    `.cluster` so a button row is a row; two elements may name the same slot.

    No `loading`, no `disabled`, no "Saving…" — a type="submit" button inside a
    <Form> reads the form's in-flight state from context and disables and spins
    on its own. Cancel does not, and must not: you abandon a save while it runs.
  -->
  <Button slot="actions" type="submit">Create order</Button>
  <Button slot="actions" variant="ghost" href="/orders/">Cancel</Button>
</Form>

<p class="text-sm text-muted">
  <code>reference</code> is <code>@upper</code> in the schema, so type it in lower case and watch what gets stored. Leave <code>note</code> empty and it saves as NULL rather than <code>''</code> — that is <code>blankToNull</code>.
</p>
